{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick","id":1373304,"title":"M5 without magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-06T19:10:17-08:00","id":1373304,"title":"M5 without magick","content":"Prediction for the M5 metaplot: The Technocracy has succeeded in strangling true magick to death with the consensus. They also run the Second Inquisition and have purchased Pentex and succeeded in killing Gaia. True magick is too mechanically confusing for newbies so only sorcerers are available as PCs and the sorcery paths work exactly like V5 disciplines (including combo paths).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T19:40:57-08:00","id":1373310,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a good enough reason to just keep playing M20 to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T20:29:47-08:00","id":1373319,"title":"","content":"Why would they make a Mage game where you can't play mages?<br /> <br /> While there's very little to go off of, the only Mage stuff Paradox/WW have done have still had mages with dynamic magic.<br /> <br /> There's just nothing to base this off on... and I say this as someone extremely skeptical of WoD5 in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T23:08:55-08:00","id":1373328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373319#post1373319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they make a Mage game where you can't play mages?<br /> <br /> While there's very little to go off of, the only Mage stuff Paradox/WW have done have still had mages with dynamic magic.<br /> <br /> There's just nothing to base this off on... and I say this as someone extremely skeptical of WoD5 in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Awakened magic is 1. was under a threat in the last edition so going by the general approach of WoD5 it\u2019s probably dead now 2. Would make the game mechanically confusing for new players which goes against the spirit of WoD5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T23:43:02-08:00","id":1373330,"title":"","content":"Awakened magick was not under a threat in M20, which made the point that the \u201cthreat\u201d that it was supposedly under in MRev was more a matter of shell-shocked mages in the immediate wake of the rose of the Avatar Storm assuming the worst. M20 emphasizes that magick is alive and well in the modern world, possibly even moreso now than it had been before the turn of the century. <br /> <br /> As for making the game less mechanically confusing, there are simpler solutions than wiping out dynamic magick; especially since the Sorcery rules are just as complicated as the Sphere Magick rules, just in a different way: switching to them wouldn't simplify the game at all. <br /> <br /> And as Tuch pointed out, if something like that were to be implemented, it would kill all interest from the existing Mage fanbase. It would also be the opposite of what V5 did: like it or hate it, V5 was an attempt to take Vampire back closer to its roots as a game of personal horror. Writing M5 as \u201cSorcerer, Third Edition\u201d would be going wildly afar from Mage's roots, not back to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-07-2020, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T23:59:35-08:00","id":1373332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373330#post1373330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened magick was not under a threat in M20, which made the point that the \u201cthreat\u201d that it was supposedly under in MRev was more a matter of shell-shocked mages in the immediate wake of the rose of the Avatar Storm assuming the worst. M20 emphasizes that magick is alive and well in the modern world, possibly even moreso now than it had been before the turn of the century. <br /> <br /> As for making the game less mechanically confusing, there are simpler solutions than wiping out dynamic magick; especially since the Sorcery rules are just as complicated as the Sphere Magick rules, just in a different way: switching to them wouldn't simplify the game at all. <br /> <br /> And as Tuch pointed out, if something like that were to be implemented, it would kill all interest from the existing Mage fanbase. It would also be the opposite of what V5 did: like it or hate it, V5 was an attempt to take Vampire back closer to its roots as a game of personal horror. Writing M5 as \u201cSorcerer, Third Edition\u201d would be going wildly afar from Mage's roots, not back to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I said they would make the sorcery paths effectively reskinned V5 disciplines.<br /> <br /> Also, they don\u2019t care about the existing Mage fanbase. V5 was one foot in the door to start selling WoD5 to new fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:02:38-08:00","id":1373333,"title":"","content":"Ah; so you're trolling. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:08:13-08:00","id":1373334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373333#post1373333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah; so you're trolling. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing with something isn\u2019t trolling? This is admittedly a pretty frivolous thread but there are plenty of those on this site. It\u2019s just my prediction for a worst case scenario if they don\u2019t learn from the criticisms of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:18:44-08:00","id":1373336,"title":"","content":"Trolling in the sense that you're trying to provoke outrage. Which I think is vastly premature, as they haven't even released W5 yet, let alone started working on M5; and as Heavy Arms said, it's without basis, as what little we <i>have</i> seen about X5's mages indicates that they still have dynamic magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:24:23-08:00","id":1373337,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not trying to provoke outrage at a nonexistent game and I don\u2019t see how this is different from other M5 speculation threads","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:30:43-08:00","id":1373338,"title":"","content":"Posting baseless assertions (one's contrary to the facts in evidence no less) to stir up negativity around M5 (a game that isn't even announced yet) is pretty bad even if it doesn't meet whatever definition of trolling you want to hide behind.<br /> <br /> My posting history speaks for itself: I think V5 is terrible, and I have zero confidence Paradox will salvage WoD5 with how they've handled things so far, and how they're proceeding in the present.<br /> <br /> If you want to speculate, even in the negative, at least bring something to the table to discuss that has some merit to it. There's a giant stack of issues we could be talking about with things they're likely to screw up that are actually present in material they've done already. Just making up the stupidest version of Mage that's still something you can imagine someone would still publish doesn't really seem to be worthwhile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T00:42:09-08:00","id":1373339,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a \u201cprediction\u201d aka speculation aka not an assertion. I think there are plenty of people who are worried about WoD5 moving in this direction and this is my idea of a \u201cworst case scenario\u201d. I didn\u2019t intend it to be any different from a thread that\u2019s like \u201chere\u2019s what I think they might do with the Nephandi in V5\u201d. But anyway this has gone totally off the rails so whatever. Also companies fundamentally prioritize profit over their products\u2019 fan bases, that\u2019s not really a ridiculous assertion to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T01:07:52-08:00","id":1373340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373339#post1373339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a \u201cprediction\u201d aka speculation aka not an assertion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's both. The following are assertions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick#post1373304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True magick is too mechanically confusing for newbies...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373328#post1373328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so going by the general approach of WoD5...<br /> Would make the game mechanically confusing for new players which goes against the spirit of WoD5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1373332#post1373332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they don\u2019t care about the existing Mage fanbase. V5 was one foot in the door to start selling WoD5 to new fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>These aren't predictions or speculations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there are plenty of people who are worried about WoD5 moving in this direction and this is my idea of a \u201cworst case scenario\u201d </div> </div> </div>There's lots of people worried about WoD5 moving in directions they don't like. I'm one of them. Even I'm not worried they're going to turn magic, the only actual reason to play mage, in Disciplines style powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also companies fundamentally prioritize profit over their products\u2019 fan bases, that\u2019s not really a ridiculous assertion to make. </div> </div> </div>Fanbase is profit in the RPG world.<br /> <br /> Paradox is off-loading development of WoD books to third parties because that increases their profits while Paradox focuses on more lucrative projects, but they still need the books to sell to fans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T07:08:19-07:00","id":1374341,"title":"","content":"Looking at the current circumstances it appears that:<br /> <br /> a) M20 still has a fair amount of mileage left in it. It was only released to the public in about 2015, and there are still supplements in the pipeline for it.<br /> b) Nobody has bought the license to develop a M5 game as of yet.<br /> c) Modiphius doesn\u2019t appear interested in any line outside of V5.<br /> d) Hunters Entertainment have only opted to develop W5 as it stands.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t really see a new edition of Mage happening for at least a couple more years, therefore. If it does happen, it may be the case that its connection to V5 and W5 might be less fully intwined as in previous editions. There will still be a WoD connection, but the references to other games may well be more downplayed.<br /> <br /> Speculation can be fun, nevertheless, but I\u2019d suggest that linking The Second Inquisition to the Technocracy and developing mages to be like sorcerers could make some good sense in V5\u2019s setting, it wouldn\u2019t necessarily impact on any future development of the Mage game proper. Indeed, there is no guarantee that anyone will see a new edition of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T16:06:06-07:00","id":1374446,"title":"","content":"Assuming they'd try to take M5 in a similar direction as V5 (which they may not--who can say?), I think they'd curtail magic heavily, but I seriously doubt they'd go to a Zero-Dynamic-Magic(k) setting.<br /> <br /> That said, Revised was already an attempt to undercut Masters (read: &quot;elders&quot;) and make the game more about street-level play, so truly the only way to go more 'down-to-earth' with it would require doing pretty extreme stuff: power levels and what can be accomplished could be capped (at the high end) at around the equivalent of having four or five dots in spheres, with none higher than Rank 3; as well as something akin to a ban on vulgar magic (i.e., rather than being more difficult, or punitive to perform vulgar effects, you simply can't do them at all). Paradox would now function like Hunger Dice, with casting literally any magical effect being equivalent to rousing the blood, and not being able to get to zero unless you've neither used, nor had magic used upon you, for a 24-hour period or something like that.<br /> <br /> I've made no secret of the fact that I'm not interested in WoD5 to the extent that it follows in the footsteps of V5 (and why wouldn't it--they're committed to the course), but this is not me trying to poo-poo V5 or the new creative direction--I'm just starting from Mage Rev. and asking myself, 'okay, how do you scale this back even <i>more</i>'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T18:48:59-07:00","id":1374470,"title":"","content":"Really, if you keep magic casting's dice pool as Arete in the V5 mechanics... you've nerfed magic by a huge degree with that alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T23:19:13-07:00","id":1374512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373304-m5-without-magick?p=1374446#post1374446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming they'd try to take M5 in a similar direction as V5 (which they may not--who can say?), I think they'd curtail magic heavily, but I seriously doubt they'd go to a Zero-Dynamic-Magic(k) setting.<br /> <br /> That said, Revised was already an attempt to undercut Masters (read: &quot;elders&quot;) and make the game more about street-level play, so truly the only way to go more 'down-to-earth' with it would require doing pretty extreme stuff: power levels and what can be accomplished could be capped (at the high end) at around the equivalent of having four or five dots in spheres, with none higher than Rank 3; as well as something akin to a ban on vulgar magic (i.e., rather than being more difficult, or punitive to perform vulgar effects, you simply can't do them at all). Paradox would now function like Hunger Dice, with casting literally any magical effect being equivalent to rousing the blood, and not being able to get to zero unless you've neither used, nor had magic used upon you, for a 24-hour period or something like that.<br /> <br /> I've made no secret of the fact that I'm not interested in WoD5 to the extent that it follows in the footsteps of V5 (and why wouldn't it--they're committed to the course), but this is not me trying to poo-poo V5 or the new creative direction--I'm just starting from Mage Rev. and asking myself, 'okay, how do you scale this back even <i>more</i>'?</div> </div> </div> </div>One possibility would be to recalibrate the Sphere scale: an Apprentice has one dot; an Initiate has two or three; a Disciple has four or five; an Adept has six or seven; a Master has eight or nine; and an Archmaster has ten. Player characters are typically assumed to work in the one to five range; but that doesn't go as far as it used to.<br /> <br /> I do think that they'd want to try out handling Paradox Backlash through something like a Hunger Dice mechanism, where the more Paradox you've built up, the more of your magic-working dice pool gets replaced by Paradox Dice that cause your magic to go askew. But I don't think they'd flat out eliminate Vulgar magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-13-2020, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}